invariant: INV-26
file: aes_extern.c
catches: quic_test_extern
reason: aes_cipher_block_256 tells ch_aes_block the key is 16 bytes, so
  every TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 block on an AES=extern object runs
  AES-128 under the first half of the traffic key. Both ends of a loop
  test run the same object and agree, so only a published answer shows
  it: FIPS 197 Appendix C.3's AES-256 block in bin/quic_test_extern,
  which the test hook computes for the length it is told.

--- old
    ch_aes_block(round_keys, AES_256_KEY, in, out);
--- new
    ch_aes_block(round_keys, AES_128_KEY, in, out);
